WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.903
Say hello to the incredible Jenna Lyons!

2
00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.298
(audience applauding)
Hi!

3
00:00:05.298 --> 00:00:06.215
Hi Jenna!

4
00:00:07.256 --> 00:00:09.410
Hi there, it's nice to see you.

5
00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:12.570
I love when you talk about how, when you were younger,

6
00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.130
you felt awkward in your skin,

7
00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:18.550
and it was when you put clothes on

8
00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:21.970
that you felt like you transformed

9
00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:24.840
into something eye-catching.

10
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:25.830
What was that like?

11
00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.150
'Cause I've never heard people talk like that.

12
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:30.533
I really love the way you put that.

13
00:00:30.533 --> 00:00:31.700
I have a genetic disorder,

14
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.780 line:15%
and the side effects of my genetic disorder

15
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.160 line:15%
are my teeth are conicular.

16
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.000 line:15%
They look like cones.

17
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.080 line:15%
I've now had them all capped, but when I was young,

18
00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:40.250 line:15%
they were not great.

19
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.570 line:15%
I also have bald spots in the back of my head,

20
00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:44.530 line:15%
and I also have scars all over my skin,

21
00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:47.180
and I was six feet tall in seventh grade.

22
00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:50.040
And all of those things combined made me

23
00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.270
not the most attractive girl in school,

24
00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:55.200
and sort of a little bit like the dork, and gawky,

25
00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.440
and awkward, and certainly not popular with the boys.

26
00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:00.100 line:15%
And I took a home economics class where I learned

27
00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.830 line:15%
how to bake cookies, I skipped the balancing the checkbook,

28
00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:04.580 line:15%
but I definitely learned how to sew,

29
00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.730 line:15%
and I made clothes for myself,

30
00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:08.270
and it was the first time anyone ever

31
00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:10.500
complimented me on how I looked.

32
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:13.770
And to go from feeling so completely

33
00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:17.230
outside of the beauty of the entire school,

34
00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:19.717
to feeling like somebody said, "Oh, I liked your skirt.

35
00:01:19.717 --> 00:01:21.120
"Can you make me one?"

36
00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.460
It was so transformational for me.

37
00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.210
Feeling confident or feeling beautiful

38
00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:26.690
can be really powerful.

39
00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:30.530
When I would first know about you so many years ago,

40
00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:33.460
you seemed so cool to me.

41
00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:37.470
So put together, so stylish, that it's really amazing to see

42
00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:40.060
someone that we've all looked to and turn to

43
00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:43.860
as a style icon, and get into that vulnerability,

44
00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:45.510
and you are on your show.

45
00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:47.870
I was riveted to that aspect.

46
00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:48.703
Thank you.

47
00:01:48.703 --> 00:01:49.580
I remember really distinctly

48
00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:51.470 line:15%
there was a board member named Heather Reisman,

49
00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:53.780 line:15%
and she was on the board when we were at J.Crew,

50
00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:57.620 line:15%
and she ran a massive business and called Indigo in Canada,

51
00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:00.080
but she asked the questions in the board meeting

52
00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:01.470
that I would have thought maybe she would have known,

53
00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:03.627
but she had no fear to say, "I'm not sure.

54
00:02:03.627 --> 00:02:04.807
"Can you explain that to me?

55
00:02:04.807 --> 00:02:06.360
"I'm not sure what this means in your business."

56
00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:09.000
And I remember feeling so like,

57
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.780
it was so clear to have somebody say," I don't understand,"

58
00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:13.617
or, "I don't know," or, "I'm not confident in this space.

59
00:02:13.617 --> 00:02:15.060
"Can you help me?"

60
00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.840
And that was empowering.

61
00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:17.940
It made me look up to her.

62
00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:20.130
It made me also realize that it's okay to do that.

63
00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:22.050
You don't have to be perfect.

64
00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:25.560
Actually, I think perfection is really not so cool.

65
00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:29.960
We wanted to see if you would impart some of your wisdom

66
00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:34.060
on a woman who I actually

67
00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:39.290
selected out of all these thousands of entries

68
00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:42.020
for our Small Business Gift Guide.

69
00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:44.920
She's the founder of Good Vibes Cookies,

70
00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:47.250
and it's a company that makes incredible

71
00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:49.670
crystal-like geode cookies.

72
00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:51.210
I'm going to bring her in.

73
00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:52.463
Hello, Jodi.

74
00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:57.400
My gosh, you're holding, oh my gosh,

75
00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.960
you're holding a citrine cookie right there.

76
00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:02.030
Okay, my mind is blown right now.

77
00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:03.940
I'm at like the trifecta.

78
00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:07.700
First of all, Drew, you broke my website.

79
00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:11.220
Like boom, crash, just not even a cookie crumb left.

80
00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:13.887
It's ridiculous, okay?
Oh, really? (squealing)

81
00:03:13.887 --> 00:03:14.720
That's amazing!

82
00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:17.620
But right now, dream come true.

83
00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:20.930
The majority of this is selling cookies.

84
00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:22.870
Do you want to stay in that lane?

85
00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:24.370
Do you wish to expand?

86
00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:27.670
What is your business fantasy?

87
00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:30.810 line:15%
The vision for Good Vibes Cookie Co

88
00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:35.810 line:15%
is into cooking, and books, maybe TV shows,

89
00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:38.170
definitely bedding, furniture.

90
00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:42.570
It's a lifestyle brand because, you know, that's who I am.

91
00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:46.130
Jenna, what do you think about sort of

92
00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:47.800
multi-pronged approach?

93
00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:50.320
Is it okay to diversify?

94
00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.110
Something to think about is

95
00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:53.660
the more complex your business is,

96
00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:55.020
the more complex your business is,

97
00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:57.730 line:15%
and the harder it is to maintain your brand identity,

98
00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:00.370 line:15%
and for people to know what you're doing and who you are.

99
00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:02.800 line:15%
So, I love the idea that you're thinking big.

100
00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:04.070
I admire that so much.

101
00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:07.310
Just give yourself a minute to get known for something

102
00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:09.990
so that people really like, it's so iconic,

103
00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:11.470
and no one else can start copying you.

104
00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:14.150
You own the space, and you do everything around it,

105
00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:16.870
and own it, and then go out and do things.

106
00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:19.350
And the other thing I would just posit for you

107
00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:21.170
is if you're going to do direct to consumer,

108
00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:22.670
it's really easy to maintain your brand,

109
00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:24.270
and your brand identity, great.

110
00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:26.090
But if you want to go wholesale, and you want to get things

111
00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:29.210
outside in a much bigger way, when you're selling to buyers,

112
00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:31.000
and you're selling them cookies and a tee shirt,

113
00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.910
it's a little harder for your story to be told in a store.

114
00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:37.170
And so that would be my only other thing to think about is

115
00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:40.100
just, you know, this is so iconic and amazing,

116
00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.690
and I don't want you to stray too far, too fast.

117
00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:44.780
Like hold for just one second, 'cause it's really cool,

118
00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:46.380
and I think there's so much more you could do with this.

119
00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:47.420
So, that would be my advice.

120
00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:51.170 line:15%
Just reconfirmed, thank you for saying that,

121
00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:54.050 line:15%
that I can do it at my own pace, and do it,

122
00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:56.110
and stay true to my brand.

123
00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:57.390
Thank you both.

124
00:04:57.390 --> 00:05:00.440 line:15%
Good Vibes Cookies is gonna be on our website.

125
00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:03.910 line:15%
It's in our Small Business Gift Guide, I'm so glad.

126
00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:07.857
Jenna Lyon, "Stylish" is streaming on HBO Max, now.

127
00:05:07.857 --> 00:05:10.274 line:15%
(pop music)

